{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The minimum value of the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-42424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/assets/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the minimum value of the function is $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-42424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-42424" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-42424" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\pi "] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["text" "There is no minimum value"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-42424" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $X+(Y-Z)$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $X+(Y-Z)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+(Y-Z) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]+([\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9-2 & 8-3 \\\\ 3-1 & 7-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4+7 & 6+5 \\\\ 2+2 & 5+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-279528" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-89052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A pet center offers veterinary services to dogs and cats. Of the total patients, $\\frac{3}{5}$\nare dogs and $\\frac{2}{5}$ are cats. Also, $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the dogs are vaccinated while $\\frac{7}{15}$ of all pets are vaccinated. What is the probability that a randomly selected cat assisted by the center is vaccinated?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-89052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $V$ be the event that the chosen pet is vaccinated, and let $D$ be the event that the pet is a dog. Then ${D}^{′}$ is the event that the pet is a cat.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected pet is vaccinated, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(V)=P(V|D)P(D)+P(V|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the pets in the center are dogs and $\\frac{2}{5}$ are cats, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=\\frac{3}{5},\\,P({D}^{′})=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the dogs are vaccinated, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|D)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{7}{15}$ of the pets are vaccinated, we have\n\n$$\nP(V)=\\frac{7}{15}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(V|{D}^{′})$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|D)P(D)+P(V|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{15} & =(\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{3}{5})+P(V|{D}^{′})(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{15} & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}P(V|{D}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}P(V|{D}^{′}) & =\\frac{7-3}{15} \\\\ P(V|{D}^{′}) & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected cat assisted in the center is vaccinated is $\\frac{2}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-89052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-89052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-89052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-89052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-7338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $8{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-4$ as a single trigonometric ratio." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-7338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n4(2{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-1)\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-1) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-7338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-7338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-7338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-7338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/assets/267d5f0aabe29da84842d2edd19276521640b838cfb1777e6932e7472716c04f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the parabola is upward-opening, has its vertex at $(2,-4),$ and passes through the point $(6,8).$\n\nWe know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola with its vertex at $(h,k),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nHere, the vertex has coordinates $(h,k)=(2,-4).$ Substituting these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}=4p(y+4).\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(6,8),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4p(y+4) \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(8+4) \\\\ 16 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4p(y+4) \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{3})(y+4) \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3}(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-11823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+4)^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}(y-2)"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}(y+4)"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(y+4)"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}(y+4)"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(y+4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-2)^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}(y+4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a controlled environment, the temperature $T$ of a food container decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the temperature. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the temperature of the container $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*In a controlled environment, the **temperature** $T$ of a food container **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the temperature.** *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *temperature $T$* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the temperature $T.$* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{T}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the temperature *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{T}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{T}^{2}},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-kT,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k{T}^{2},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{T}^{2}},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k{T}^{2},\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{T}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-101541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-101541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{13}⟨0,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{6}{13}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-101541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-101541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-101541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\frac{2}{13},\\frac{3}{13}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\frac{2}{73},\\frac{3}{73}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{6}{13}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\frac{4}{73},\\frac{6}{73}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-101541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{6}{13}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-116604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{3}-9x<0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-116604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the polynomial on the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-9x & =x({x}^{2}-9) \\\\  & =x(x+3)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we define the function $f(x)$ as\n\n$$\nf(x)=x(x+3)(x-3).\n$$\n\nSo we're now solving the inequality $f(x)<0.$\n\nThe solutions to the equation $f(x)=0$ are $x=-3,$ $x=0$ and $x=3.$ These roots divide the number line into $4$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-3),\\,(-3,0),\\,(0,3),\\,(3,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(-3,0)$ | $(0,3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+3$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)<0,$ we look at the bottom row to determine where $f(x)$ is negative.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-3)$ and $(0,3).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-116604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-116604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-116604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,3)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (0,3)"] ["math" "x\\in (3,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-116604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}k & k \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot 1-k\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =k-2k \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k & =0 \\\\ k & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95"} {"question" "q-11723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "k=-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "k=0"] ["math" "k=\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "k=\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "91185d5bb2f69b011ef412b624fa1f05b8a408a0c4b78b6ff40f6212d1d11c9a"} {"question" "q-11723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home